        transliteration: 'rāmo vigrahavān dharmaḥ sādhuḥ satyaparākramaḥ |\nrājā sarvasya lokasya devānām iva vāsavaḥ ||',
        translation: 'Rama is dharma in bodily form, virtuous, whose valour is truth; he is the king of the whole world, as Indra is of the gods.',
