        transliteration: 'sa papāta kharo bhūmau dahyamānaḥ śarāgninā |\nrudreṇeva vinirdagdhaḥ śvetāraṇye yathāndhakaḥ ||',
        translation: 'Khara fell to the ground, burning in the fire of the arrow, like Andhaka consumed by Rudra in the White Forest.',
